    "description": "Literal types are types which not only check the type of a value but also the value itself. PHP has support for two literal types: false as of PHP 8.0.0, and true as of PHP 8.2.0.",
    "code": "<?php\n\n    // bool is a type\n    // false is a literal type : a bool, which value is false\n    function trumpet(bool $a) : false {\n        return false;\n    }\n\n?>",
